## Impact
The increaseLiquidity function in the NonfungiblePositionManager contract lacks an authorization check, specifically the isAuthorizedForToken(params.tokenId) modifier. This omission allows any registered external caller to increase the liquidity of any NFT position without proper authorization, potentially leading to unauthorized manipulation of liquidity positions. In the NonfungiblePositionManager contract, the decreaseLiquidity function is protected by the isAuthorizedForToken(params.tokenId) modifier, ensuring that only the owner or an approved operator can decrease the liquidity of a specific NFT position. However, the increaseLiquidity function does not implement this modifier, leaving it unprotected. This inconsistency allows any registered user to call increaseLiquidity on any token ID, enabling them to manipulate the liquidity of positions they do not own or control. 

